  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 8.2. Increased capacity of member States to improve governance and sustainability of social protection systems</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) Government of Malawi (GoM), Ministry of Gender, Community Development and Social Welfare (MGCDSW) developed the social cash transfer strategy between October 2020 and June 2021. Government will operationalise the strategy by December 2021. An action plan was developed in 2020 to improve implementation and administration of social protection service delivery. 
(2) GoM developed a social protection Monitoring and Evaluation (M&amp;E) Framework in November 2020. It is expected to be adopted by 31 December 2021. It will support regular collection, compilation and statistical monitoring of both contributory and non-contributory social protection programmes.  
(3) The MGCDSW  operationalized an assessment and registration mechanism to identify and bring on board beneficiaries of the COVID 19 Urban Cash Intervention (CUCI) in Malawi&#x2019;s two major cities, Lilongwe and Zomba. Between March and July 2021, over 95,000 households, representing 378,000 individuals were assessed and enrolled into the CUCI. 
(4) The MGCDSW enhanced the capacity of 15 Senior government Officials in April 2021 through the new TRANSFORM Shock Responsive Module. Sensitizations took place in in 9 districts. GoM has adopted the TRANSFORM package in the management of Social Protection Programmes, and will by December 2021 institutionalize the TRANSFORM Training package in social protection training institutions. (1)ILO provided technical   support to the MGCDSW to conduct consultation meetings at district, regional and national level. 
ILO provided technical support for the development of the action plan for the strategy.
(2) The ILO provided support to the capacity development of Ministry of Economic Planning, Development and Public Sector Reforms data collectors. The ILO provided technical support to the development of the  M&amp;E assessment processes. The ILO provided technical support to consultative meetings with government  and national partners.
(3) The ILO provided support to the government to develop a rapid assessment and registration criteria for the COVID 19 Urban Cash Interventions (CUCI). The methodology applied innovative targeting techniques applying a blend of geographical mapping and on-ground vulnerability assessment exercises.
(4) The ILO coordinated development and online application of the TRANSFORM Shock Responsive Module in May 2021; and conducted TRANSFORM training workshops for national and district Officials and policy makers. 
The ILO in August 2021 conducted a Training for a new TRANSFORM Finance &amp; Financial Management module using a blended training format.</narrative>
   </description>
